**Key findings so far:**

1. **Blood culture sensitivity ~30-40% in LMIC neonates** (BARNARDS 25.1% culture-pos, NeoOBS 17.7%, ANISA culture:modeled ~12%). 50-80% of truly bacterially infected neonates have negative cultures.

2. **No consensus CRS exists.** 128 definitions across 80 RCTs. WHO TPP is **silent on reference standard** — the single most exploitable gap in NeoTest AMC design.

3. **NeoSep-SAA's 92% Se is against clinical judgment** (broadest standard). Against a stringent CRS: projected ~77-87% Se (central ~82%) — **fails the non-hospital TPP minimum of ≥90%**. SAA meta-analysis pooled Se=0.85 also fails non-hospital threshold.

4. **Three gaming risks** + model misalignment (UChicago model uses true-bacterial-prevalence denominator, milestone reference undefined). **Six AMC milestone fixes** needed: pre-locked CRS, independent adjudication, neonatal-capillary validation, culture-neg subgroup sizing, LCA secondary, prohibit clinical-only validation.

